    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35709" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perversĭtas</span></b> ,
		ātis, f.
		perversus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>frowardness</i>, <i>untowardness</i>,
				<i>perversity</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae est autem in hominibus tanta perversitas,
					ut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Or. 9, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opinionum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 3, 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magna perversitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Off. 1, 40, 145</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicujus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q. Fr. 1, 1, 13, § 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">molestissima diligentiae perversitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 6, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incredibilis hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 1, 7, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
